{
  "schemaVersion": "explainer-kit.author-result/v2",
  "artifactId": "project-recap",
  "content": {
    "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n    <title>Wave 1: test and CI containment</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Two small defects, a smoke harness that could hang forever and a release gate that could pass a stale version, fixed and merged as one wrapper project.\" />\n    <style>\n      :root {\n        --canvas: #f4f6f9;\n          --panel: #ffffff;\n          --elevated: #eef1f5;\n          --border: color-mix(in srgb, #4a5568 26%, transparent);\n          --ink: #16202e;\n          --muted: #4a5568;\n          --accent: #2f56c9;\n          --accent-2: #0e7180;\n          --success: #157a54;\n          --warning: #965108;\n          --danger: #bd3a2c;\n        --sans: system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif;\n        --serif: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;\n        --mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Consolas, monospace;\n        --radius: 8px;\n        --radius-lg: 12px;\n        --rule: 1px solid var(--border);\n        --measure: 66ch;\n      }\n      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n        :root {\n          --canvas: #111827;\n          --panel: #1f2937;\n          --elevated: #374151;\n          --border: color-mix(in srgb, #d1d5db 26%, transparent);\n          --ink: #f9fafb;\n          --muted: #d1d5db;\n          --accent: #93c5fd;\n          --accent-2: #5eead4;\n          --success: #86efac;\n          --warning: #fde047;\n          --danger: #fca5a5;\n        }\n      }\n      * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n      html {\n        color-scheme: light dark;\n        scroll-behavior: smooth;\n      }\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        background: var(--canvas);\n        color: var(--ink);\n        font-family: var(--sans);\n        font-size: 1rem;\n        line-height: 1.65;\n        -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;\n      }\n      a { color: var(--accent); }\n      a:focus-visible,\n      .toc a:focus-visible {\n        outline: 2px solid var(--accent);\n        outline-offset: 2px;\n      }\n      .wrap {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(11rem, 15rem) minmax(0, 1fr);\n        gap: 2.5rem;\n        max-width: 76rem;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n        padding: 2.5rem 2rem 4rem;\n      }\n      main { min-width: 0; }\n\n      /* Typographic roles */\n      .eyebrow,\n      .toc-label,\n      .label {\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n      h1 {\n        font-family: var(--serif);\n        font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 6vw, 3.4rem);\n        font-weight: 600;\n        line-height: 1.08;\n        letter-spacing: -0.015em;\n        margin: 0.6rem 0 0;\n        text-wrap: balance;\n      }\n      .lede {\n        font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2.4vw, 1.3rem);\n        line-height: 1.5;\n        max-width: 46ch;\n        margin: 1rem 0 0;\n        color: var(--ink);\n      }\n      h2 {\n        font-family: var(--serif);\n        font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3.2vw, 1.9rem);\n        font-weight: 600;\n        line-height: 1.15;\n        margin: 0 0 1.1rem;\n        padding-bottom: 0.5rem;\n        border-bottom: var(--rule);\n        scroll-margin-top: 1.5rem;\n        text-wrap: balance;\n      }\n      h3 {\n        font-family: var(--sans);\n        font-size: 1.05rem;\n        font-weight: 650;\n        line-height: 1.3;\n        margin: 0 0 0.4rem;\n      }\n      p { margin: 0 0 1rem; max-width: var(--measure); }\n      .note {\n        font-size: 0.875rem;\n        line-height: 1.5;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n      code, pre { font-family: var(--mono); }\n      :not(pre) > code {\n        font-size: 0.86em;\n        background: var(--elevated);\n        border-radius: 4px;\n        padding: 0.08em 0.32em;\n        overflow-wrap: anywhere;\n      }\n\n      /* Navigation rail */\n      .toc {\n        position: sticky;\n        top: 2rem;\n        align-self: start;\n        max-height: calc(100dvh - 4rem);\n        overflow-y: auto;\n      }\n      .toc-label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }\n      .toc ol {\n        list-style: none;\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        counter-reset: toc;\n      }\n      .toc a {\n        display: block;\n        border-left: 2px solid var(--border);\n        padding: 0.32rem 0 0.32rem 0.75rem;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        font-size: 0.9rem;\n        line-height: 1.35;\n        text-decoration: none;\n      }\n      .toc a:hover { color: var(--ink); }\n      .toc a.active {\n        border-left-color: var(--accent);\n        color: var(--ink);\n        font-weight: 650;\n      }\n\n      /* Masthead and status */\n      .masthead { margin-bottom: 3rem; }\n      .status-strip {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 9.5rem), 1fr));\n        gap: 1px;\n        background: var(--border);\n        border: var(--rule);\n        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n        overflow: hidden;\n        margin-top: 2rem;\n      }\n      .stat {\n        background: var(--panel);\n        padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem;\n      }\n      .stat .label { display: block; }\n      .stat b {\n        display: block;\n        font-family: var(--serif);\n        font-size: 1.45rem;\n        font-weight: 600;\n        line-height: 1.15;\n        margin-top: 0.25rem;\n      }\n      .stat.is-good b { color: var(--success); }\n      .stat span.sub {\n        display: block;\n        font-size: 0.8rem;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n\n      section { margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }\n\n      /* Section 1: contract */\n      .contract {\n        list-style: none;\n        margin: 1.5rem 0 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        display: grid;\n        gap: 0.65rem;\n        max-width: var(--measure);\n      }\n      .contract li {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: 1.6rem 1fr;\n        gap: 0.6rem;\n        align-items: baseline;\n      }\n      .contract li::before {\n        content: counter(rule);\n        counter-increment: rule;\n        font: 700 0.7rem/1.6 var(--mono);\n        color: var(--accent);\n      }\n      .contract { counter-reset: rule; }\n\n      /* Section 2: decisions */\n      .decisions {\n        list-style: none;\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        counter-reset: decision;\n        display: grid;\n        gap: 1.6rem;\n      }\n      .decisions > li {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: 2.6rem minmax(0, 1fr);\n        gap: 0.4rem 1rem;\n        padding-top: 1.2rem;\n        border-top: var(--rule);\n      }\n      .decisions > li::before {\n        content: counter(decision, decimal-leading-zero);\n        counter-increment: decision;\n        font: 600 1.4rem/1 var(--serif);\n        color: var(--accent);\n      }\n      .decisions h3 { grid-column: 2; }\n      .decisions dl {\n        grid-column: 2;\n        margin: 0.5rem 0 0;\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);\n        gap: 0.5rem 1.2rem;\n        max-width: var(--measure);\n      }\n      .decisions dt {\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n      }\n      .decisions dd { margin: 0.1rem 0 0; }\n      @media (min-width: 52rem) {\n        .decisions dl { grid-template-columns: 5.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); }\n        .decisions dt { text-align: right; padding-top: 0.28rem; }\n        .decisions dd { margin-top: 0; }\n      }\n\n      /* Section 3: architecture */\n      figure { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; }\n      .diagram-scroll {\n        max-width: 100%;\n        overflow-x: auto;\n        border: var(--rule);\n        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n        background: var(--canvas);\n        padding: 1rem;\n      }\n      svg.diagram {\n        display: block;\n        width: 100%;\n        min-width: 40rem;\n        height: auto;\n      }\n      .diagram .node { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }\n      .diagram .node.is-lane { fill: var(--elevated); stroke: var(--accent); }\n      .diagram .node.is-goal { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--success); stroke-width: 2; }\n      .diagram .edge { fill: none; stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 2; }\n      .diagram .edge.is-feedback { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-dasharray: 6 5; }\n      .diagram .arrow { fill: var(--accent); }\n      .diagram .arrow.is-muted { fill: var(--muted); }\n      .diagram .node-label {\n        fill: var(--ink);\n        font: 650 14px var(--sans);\n      }\n      .diagram .node-sub {\n        fill: var(--muted);\n        font: 11px var(--mono);\n      }\n      .diagram .edge-label {\n        fill: var(--muted);\n        font: 11px var(--mono);\n      }\n      figcaption {\n        margin-top: 0.75rem;\n        font-size: 0.875rem;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        max-width: var(--measure);\n      }\n      .lanes {\n        display: grid;\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 17rem), 1fr));\n        gap: 1.25rem;\n        margin-top: 2rem;\n      }\n      .lane {\n        min-width: 0;\n        border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);\n        padding-top: 0.9rem;\n      }\n      .lane.is-secondary { border-top-color: var(--muted); }\n      .lane ul { margin: 0.6rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; }\n      .lane li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }\n\n      /* Tables */\n      .table-scroll {\n        max-width: 100%;\n        overflow-x: auto;\n        margin-top: 1.4rem;\n      }\n      table {\n        width: 100%;\n        min-width: 38rem;\n        border-collapse: collapse;\n        font-size: 0.94rem;\n      }\n      caption {\n        text-align: left;\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.14em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        padding-bottom: 0.6rem;\n      }\n      th, td {\n        border-bottom: var(--rule);\n        padding: 0.62rem 0.9rem 0.62rem 0;\n        text-align: left;\n        vertical-align: top;\n      }\n      thead th {\n        font: 700 0.68rem/1.4 var(--mono);\n        letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n        text-transform: uppercase;\n        color: var(--muted);\n        border-bottom-width: 2px;\n      }\n      tbody th { font-weight: 650; white-space: nowrap; }\n      td.evidence { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); }\n      td.ok { color: var(--success); }\n\n      /* Section 6: outcome */\n      .outcome {\n        display: grid;\n        gap: 1.75rem;\n        margin-top: 0.5rem;\n      }\n      .outcome > div { max-width: var(--measure); }\n      .outcome h3 { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.55rem; }\n      .outcome h3 .label { letter-spacing: 0.14em; }\n      .outcome ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.15rem; }\n      .outcome li { margin-bottom: 0.45rem; }\n      .outcome .works { border-left: 3px solid var(--success); padding-left: 1rem; }\n      .outcome .gaps { border-left: 3px solid var(--warning); padding-left: 1rem; }\n      .outcome .next { border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 1rem; }\n\n      footer {\n        margin-top: 3.5rem;\n        padding-top: 1.2rem;\n        border-top: var(--rule);\n        color: var(--muted);\n        font-size: 0.85rem;\n      }\n      footer p { max-width: var(--measure); }\n\n      @media (max-width: 52rem) {\n        .wrap {\n          grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);\n          gap: 1.25rem;\n          padding: 1rem 1rem 3rem;\n        }\n        .toc {\n          position: sticky;\n          top: 0;\n          z-index: 2;\n          max-height: none;\n          overflow-x: auto;\n          overflow-y: hidden;\n          background: var(--canvas);\n          border-bottom: var(--rule);\n          padding: 0.6rem 0;\n          margin: 0 -1rem;\n          padding-left: 1rem;\n          padding-right: 1rem;\n        }\n        .toc-label { display: none; }\n        .toc ol { display: flex; gap: 0.3rem; }\n        .toc a {\n          flex: none;\n          white-space: nowrap;\n          border-left: 0;\n          border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);\n          padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem;\n          font-size: 0.82rem;\n        }\n        .toc a.active { border-bottom-color: var(--accent); border-left-color: transparent; }\n        .decisions > li { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }\n        .decisions > li::before { grid-column: 1; }\n        .decisions h3, .decisions dl { grid-column: 1; }\n      }\n      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n        html { scroll-behavior: auto; }\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div class=\"wrap\">\n      <nav class=\"toc\" aria-label=\"Recap sections\">\n        <span class=\"toc-label\">OAT project recap / shared / wave-1-execution</span>\n        <ol>\n          <li><a href=\"#original-request\">What was asked for</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#key-agent-decisions\">Decisions that shaped the result</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#as-built-architecture\">How the wave was built</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#implementation-record\">What changed</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#validation-evidence\">How it was checked</a></li>\n          <li><a href=\"#outcome\">Where this leaves the repository</a></li>\n        </ol>\n      </nav>\n      <main>\n        <header class=\"masthead\">\n          <span class=\"eyebrow\">OAT project recap / shared / wave-1-execution</span>\n          <h1>Wave 1: test and CI containment</h1>\n          <p class=\"lede\">Two small defects, a smoke test harness that could hang forever and a release gate that could pass a stale version, were fixed and merged as one wrapper project.</p>\n          <div class=\"status-strip\">\n            <div class=\"stat is-good\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Wave 1</span>\n              <b>Complete</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">both phases merged</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Lanes</span>\n              <b>2 of 2</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">run in parallel, merged in order</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat is-good\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Definition of done</span>\n              <b>Green</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">10 gates, every exit code 0</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"stat is-good\">\n              <span class=\"label\">Reviews</span>\n              <b>Passed</b>\n              <span class=\"sub\">phase, final and exit gate</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </header>\n        <section id=\"original-request\" aria-labelledby=\"original-request-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"original-request-heading\">What was asked for</h2>\n          <p>Wave 1 of the 2026-08-19 execution program asked for two recently observed, small defects to be closed together as one thin wrapper OAT project. The wrapper owned ordering, worktree isolation, gates, review mapping and bookkeeping. Nothing else.</p>\n          <p>Each lane kept its entire implementation contract in its own immutable external plan. The wrapper was forbidden from restating, narrowing or overriding any of it, which is what separates the request from the eventual implementation: the request is a routing and safety problem, the implementation lives in the two source plans.</p>\n          <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n            <table>\n              <caption>The two lanes and the defects they close</caption>\n              <thead>\n                <tr><th scope=\"col\">Lane</th><th scope=\"col\">Defect</th><th scope=\"col\">External plan</th></tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">p01</th>\n                  <td>The smoke cleanup SIGTERM regression harness could wait forever on a child that ignored the signal, wedging <code>pnpm test</code>.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">2026-08-19-bound-smoke-cleanup-signal-wait.md</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">p02</th>\n                  <td>A long-lived branch whose lockstep bump had been overtaken by a later release on <code>main</code> still passed CI.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">2026-08-19-detect-behind-main-package-versions.md</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <h3>The constraints the wrapper accepted</h3>\n          <ol class=\"contract\">\n            <li>Run each source plan's drift check against current HEAD before touching code. A material mismatch stops the lane.</li>\n            <li>Honour every source-plan STOP condition verbatim. A tripped STOP parks the lane instead of weakening the plan.</li>\n            <li>Confirm the source plan's own done criteria, then run the full definition of done and capture every exit code explicitly.</li>\n            <li>Keep reviewed history append-only. Fix rounds land as new commits; no reviewed SHA is amended.</li>\n            <li>Merge phase branches one at a time in plan order, and do backlog archival once on the integration branch after every merge.</li>\n          </ol>\n          <p class=\"note\">Success meant both plans' done criteria confirmed and recorded, every review row <code>passed</code>, the full definition of done green, and the wave merged to <code>main</code>.</p>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"key-agent-decisions\" aria-labelledby=\"key-agent-decisions-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"key-agent-decisions-heading\">Decisions that shaped the result</h2>\n          <p>Four choices changed what shipped. Each is recorded with the reason it was made and the consequence it carried.</p>\n          <ol class=\"decisions\">\n            <li>\n              <h3>Run both lanes as one parallel group</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>The wave-boundary drift refresh found an empty write-surface intersection. p01 only touches <code>tools/smoke</code>; p02 only touches <code>tools/release</code> and <code>packages/cli/src/release</code>.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>Two worktrees started from the same base and merged in plan order, p01 first, so the bounded signal harness was already in place for the release lane’s integration test run.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <h3>Take a wave-level lockstep bump instead of exempting test paths</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>Test files under <code>packages/cli/src</code> count as publishable changes, so the repository guardrail demanded a five-package bump that neither lane could make on its own.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>The root bumped 0.2.32 to 0.2.33 once after fan-in, which also exercised the new guard’s green path. Editing <code>versionPolicyIgnorePatterns</code> was rejected as a policy decision outside the plan.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <h3>Reconcile the release-guard plan without narrowing it</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>The plan scopes the strict-greater comparison to <code>check-version-bumps.ts</code> and <code>release-utils.ts</code>, and forbids adding a second competing gate.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>The new errors were appended to the result that already aggregates the merge-base lockstep errors, so one run names every required rebase or re-bump. The separate lockstep pass in <code>release:validate</code> was left alone.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n            <li>\n              <h3>Merge phase branches without rebasing them</h3>\n              <dl>\n                <dt>Reason</dt>\n                <dd>The phase branches touched only code and the integration branch touched only <code>.oat/projects</code>, so there was nothing to replay.</dd>\n                <dt>Consequence</dt>\n                <dd>A plain <code>git merge --no-ff</code> in plan order preserved every reviewed SHA that the review chain cites.</dd>\n              </dl>\n            </li>\n          </ol>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"as-built-architecture\" aria-labelledby=\"as-built-architecture-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"as-built-architecture-heading\">How the wave was built</h2>\n          <p>The delivered system is two independent code changes plus the machinery that carried them from the program document to <code>main</code>. The wrapper owns that path. The external plans own what each lane writes.</p>\n          <figure>\n            <div class=\"diagram-scroll\">\n              <svg class=\"diagram\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 684\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"arch-title arch-desc\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMin meet\">\n                <title id=\"arch-title\">Wave 1 execution architecture</title>\n                <desc id=\"arch-desc\">The 2026-08-19 execution program scopes the wave-1-execution wrapper project. The wrapper dispatches two parallel lanes, p01 for the smoke cleanup harness and p02 for the release version guard. Both merge into one integration branch, which then receives the lockstep bump, the ten definition-of-done gates and the final reviews before the wave merges to main. A dashed feedback edge runs from the gates and reviews back into lane p01 for the final-review fix.</desc>\n                <defs>\n                  <marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n                    <path class=\"arrow\" d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" />\n                  </marker>\n                  <marker id=\"arrow-muted\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n                    <path class=\"arrow is-muted\" d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z\" />\n                  </marker>\n                </defs>\n                <g>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"330\" y=\"16\" width=\"240\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"40\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2026-08-19 execution program</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"57\" text-anchor=\"middle\">four waves, immutable</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"290\" y=\"112\" width=\"320\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wave-1-execution</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"middle\">wrapper OAT project, quick mode</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node is-lane\" x=\"24\" y=\"212\" width=\"372\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"210\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lane p01 worktree</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"210\" y=\"257\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bound smoke cleanup signal waits</text>\n                  <text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"210\" y=\"274\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tools/smoke/runner/cleanup.test.mjs</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node is-lane\" x=\"504\" y=\"212\" width=\"372\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"690\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lane p02 worktree</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"690\" y=\"257\" text-anchor=\"middle\">reject versions overtaken by main</text>\n                  <text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"690\" y=\"274\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tools/release, packages/cli/src/release</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"290\" y=\"340\" width=\"320\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"364\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Integration branch</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"381\" text-anchor=\"middle\">fan-in, backlog archival</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"290\" y=\"428\" width=\"320\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"452\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lockstep bump 0.2.33</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"469\" text-anchor=\"middle\">five public packages, root owned</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node\" x=\"290\" y=\"516\" width=\"320\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"540\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 gates and reviews</text><text class=\"node-sub\" x=\"450\" y=\"557\" text-anchor=\"middle\">definition of done, final, exit gate</text>\n                  <rect class=\"node is-goal\" x=\"330\" y=\"604\" width=\"240\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" />\n                  <text class=\"node-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"631\" text-anchor=\"middle\">main</text>\n                </g>\n                <g>\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,68 V112\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,164 V188 H210 V212\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,164 V188 H690 V212\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M210,292 V316 H450 V340\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M690,292 V316 H450 V340\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,392 V428\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,480 V516\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M450,568 V604\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\" />\n                  <path class=\"edge is-feedback\" d=\"M290,542 H14 V252 H24\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow-muted)\" />\n                </g>\n                <g>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"94\">scopes the wave</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dispatched in parallel, disjoint write surfaces</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"450\" y=\"308\" text-anchor=\"middle\">merged one at a time, p01 then p02</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"414\">repository guardrail</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"502\">re-run after the bump</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"462\" y=\"590\">wave PR</text>\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"30\" y=\"532\">final-review fix p01-t02</text>\n                </g>\n                <g>\n                  <path class=\"edge\" d=\"M24,676 H56\" />\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"64\" y=\"680\">promotion and merge</text>\n                  <path class=\"edge is-feedback\" d=\"M230,676 H262\" />\n                  <text class=\"edge-label\" x=\"270\" y=\"680\">review feedback</text>\n                </g>\n              </svg>\n            </div>\n            <figcaption>Flow of the wave. The wrapper fans out into two isolated worktrees, fans back in on the integration branch, and only then applies the repository-mandated lockstep bump and re-runs the gates. The dashed edge is the one review finding that reopened a lane after fan-in.</figcaption>\n          </figure>\n          <div class=\"lanes\">\n            <div class=\"lane\">\n              <h3>What the wrapper owns</h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Phase ordering, grouping and the concurrency ceiling</li>\n                <li>Worktree isolation and merge serialisation</li>\n                <li>Wrapper-level gates and the review mapping</li>\n                <li>Commit scope naming and all bookkeeping</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"lane is-secondary\">\n              <h3>What each external plan owns</h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Its drift check and STOP conditions</li>\n                <li>Its implementation steps and embedded verify gates</li>\n                <li>Its done criteria and review focus</li>\n                <li>The files it is allowed to write</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <h3>Delivered surfaces</h3>\n          <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n            <table>\n              <caption>As-built boundaries</caption>\n              <thead>\n                <tr><th scope=\"col\">Surface</th><th scope=\"col\">Responsibility after the wave</th></tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>tools/smoke/runner/cleanup.test.mjs</code></th>\n                  <td>Bounded wait, force-kill and reap-or-detach helpers with injectable test seams, plus the regression tests that hold them in place.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>tools/release/release-utils.ts</code></th>\n                  <td>Resolves the current <code>origin/main</code> ref, separately from the merge base, and compares numeric <code>major.minor.patch</code> versions.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>tools/release/check-version-bumps.ts</code></th>\n                  <td>Runs the existing merge-base lockstep rule first, then appends the strict-greater errors to the same report.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\"><code>packages/cli/src/release/</code></th>\n                  <td>Regression suites for the comparator and the gate, including the overtaken-main case.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Public package manifests</th>\n                  <td>Five packages plus the generated <code>public-package-versions.json</code>, all at 0.2.33.</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"implementation-record\" aria-labelledby=\"implementation-record-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"implementation-record-heading\">What changed</h2>\n          <p>Both lanes landed as append-only commit chains. Fix rounds are separate commits, so every SHA a review cites still resolves.</p>\n          <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n            <table>\n              <caption>Implementation record</caption>\n              <thead>\n                <tr><th scope=\"col\">Component</th><th scope=\"col\">Notable change</th><th scope=\"col\">Commits</th></tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Smoke cleanup harness</th>\n                  <td>Every child-exit await in <code>runSignalCase</code> is bounded at 60 seconds. A missed SIGTERM triggers SIGKILL and a bounded 15 second reap before temp-dir cleanup. An unreapable child is detached rather than left stalling the event loop. The success assertion is unchanged.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">aedced64, 6a9ed1af, fd8c7cb9</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Fixture determinism</th>\n                  <td>The generated SIGTERM-ignoring wrapper now installs its handler at module scope before it writes the sentinel the parent waits on, closing a race the parent could win.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">196dae19</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Release version guard</th>\n                  <td><code>pnpm release:check-versions</code> also rejects any lockstep version that is not strictly greater than <code>origin/main</code>. Malformed or missing evidence fails closed, and the comparison never runs when no publishable roots changed.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">c8fdefc3, b486beb6</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Lockstep bump</th>\n                  <td>Five public package manifests and the generated <code>public-package-versions.json</code> moved from 0.2.32 to 0.2.33 on the integration branch.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">4fa530e6</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Fan-in and bookkeeping</th>\n                  <td>p01 merged first, then p02. Backlog archival ran once afterwards, closing both tracked items in a single commit.</td>\n                  <td class=\"evidence\">c5c32345, 872a06be, 848beb88</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"note\">Neither lane changed shipped package versions itself. The bump is a separate, root-owned commit for exactly that reason.</p>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"validation-evidence\" aria-labelledby=\"validation-evidence-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"validation-evidence-heading\">How it was checked</h2>\n          <p>The interesting evidence is not that the suite passed. It is that both lanes were probed adversarially, and that the two defects the wave targeted are demonstrably red without the fixes.</p>\n          <div class=\"table-scroll\">\n            <table>\n              <caption>Validation evidence</caption>\n              <thead>\n                <tr><th scope=\"col\">Check</th><th scope=\"col\">Where it ran</th><th scope=\"col\">Observed result</th><th scope=\"col\">Limits</th></tr>\n              </thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Smoke harness suite</th>\n                  <td><code>node --test tools/smoke/runner/cleanup.test.mjs</code> at the final head</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Exit 0. 19 tests pass, 0 cancelled, 12.76 seconds.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">The per-case deadline is 60 seconds, roughly 35 times the typical run.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Full smoke tier</th>\n                  <td><code>pnpm test:smoke</code> at the final head</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Exit 0. 139 pass, 0 fail.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">One reviewer run failed earlier in the pre-existing deterministic tier on a shared-git worktree collision and passed on an isolated rerun.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Mutation battery</th>\n                  <td>p01 review rounds, delete-class and reorder-class mutations</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Every mutation is red without the fixes, including the reorder case that the delete class missed.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Reviewer-designed, not part of the committed suite.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Release regression suites</th>\n                  <td>Focused suites under <code>packages/cli/src/release/</code></td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">43 tests pass. The 0.2.29 branch against 0.2.30 main case is red, and the same test asserts the old merge-base rule alone would have passed it.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">The missing-ref branch is reachable only through dependency injection, because the pre-existing no-merge-base skip shadows it.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Live gate probe</th>\n                  <td>Exit-gate reviewer, dependency-injected versions against the real gate</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">0.2.32 failed with 6 errors, 0.2.31 failed with 5, 0.2.34 passed, 0.2.33-rc.1 failed with 5.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Prereleases are rejected by the comparator rather than coerced.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Definition of done</th>\n                  <td>Integration head, 10 gates captured individually</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Every exit code 0: check, type-check, test at 144 seconds with 3672 vitest and 39 node:test cases, build, check:skill-bumps, release:check-versions, release:validate, build:docs, lint and format.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\"><code>release:check-versions</code> needs a current <code>origin/main</code> ref. CI checks out at full depth; locally, fetch first.</td>\n                </tr>\n                <tr>\n                  <th scope=\"row\">Reviews</th>\n                  <td>p01 three rounds, p02 two rounds, final two rounds, plus the configured exit gate</td>\n                  <td class=\"ok\">Every row passed. The exit gate reported 0 critical, 0 important, 0 medium and 2 minor findings.</td>\n                  <td class=\"note\">Three minor findings were re-verified and deliberately deferred rather than closed.</td>\n                </tr>\n              </tbody>\n            </table>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"note\">The two findings that mattered, an unsettleable post-detach reap and a fixture ordering race, were found by reviewer-designed probes and mutation runs. Every implementer gate and cross-model pass was green at the time.</p>\n        </section>\n        <section id=\"outcome\" aria-labelledby=\"outcome-heading\">\n          <h2 id=\"outcome-heading\">Where this leaves the repository</h2>\n          <div class=\"outcome\">\n            <div class=\"works\">\n              <h3><span class=\"label\">Works now</span></h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>A smoke child that ignores SIGTERM is force-killed, reaped or detached, and reported with its paused stage and captured output. The suite fails in about a minute instead of never.</li>\n                <li>CI rejects a pull request whose public package versions equal or trail <code>origin/main</code>, naming every affected package in one run alongside the existing merge-base errors.</li>\n                <li>Both tracked backlog items are closed, and the repository sits at 0.2.33 across the five public packages.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"gaps\">\n              <h3><span class=\"label\">Did not ship</span></h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Nothing either source plan required was dropped or narrowed.</li>\n                <li>Three minor findings remain deferred: quote whitespace in the malformed-version diagnostic, regression coverage for the forced and timed-out diagnostic branches, and the zombie-child wording.</li>\n                <li>The documentation for the new strictly-above-main rule was routed to the documentation step rather than deferred.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"next\">\n              <h3><span class=\"label\">For the next reader</span></h3>\n              <ul>\n                <li>Fetch <code>origin/main</code> before running <code>pnpm release:check-versions</code> locally, or the gate has no current ref to compare against.</li>\n                <li>Any change under <code>packages/cli/src</code>, tests included, triggers the lockstep bump requirement. Plan that bump before a lane starts, not after fan-in.</li>\n                <li>Pick up the deferred minors on the next release-tooling or smoke-harness touch.</li>\n                <li>Waves 2 to 4 baseline their versions on whatever <code>origin/main</code> holds when that wave starts.</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </section>\n        <footer>\n          <p>Recap built from the approved lifecycle artifacts of the OAT project <code>.oat/projects/shared/wave-1-execution</code>: <code>plan.md</code>, <code>implementation.md</code> and <code>summary.md</code>. Commit references are short SHAs on the wave integration branch. Line and file pointers quoted in those artifacts shift with later edits and should be verified against HEAD.</p>\n        </footer>\n      </main>\n    </div>\n<script>\n      (() => {\n        const links = [...document.querySelectorAll('.toc a[href^=\"#\"]')];\n        const targets = links\n          .map((link) => document.querySelector(link.getAttribute('href')))\n          .filter(Boolean);\n        const observer = new IntersectionObserver(\n          (entries) => {\n            for (const entry of entries) {\n              if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;\n              links.forEach((link) =>\n                link.classList.toggle(\n                  'active',\n                  link.getAttribute('href') === `#${entry.target.id}`,\n                ),\n              );\n            }\n          },\n          { rootMargin: '-15% 0px -70% 0px' },\n        );\n        targets.forEach((target) => observer.observe(target));\n      })();\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
